=== D1-39 Detailed Investigation ===

Test 1: spawnSync('npm.cmd') WITHOUT shell:true
  error: EINVAL
  status: null
  stdout: (empty)

Test 2: spawnSync('npm.cmd') WITH shell:true
  error: none
  status: 0
  stdout: {
  "next": "1.1.6-next.0",
  "latest": "1.1.5"
}


Test 3: queryDistTagsSync() from update-check.mjs
  result: null

=== VERDICT: BUG CONFIRMED ===
Root cause: update-check.mjs L238 queryDistTagsSync uses spawnSync('npm.cmd') without shell:true
  -> On Windows, spawnSync of .cmd files requires shell:true (Node.js known issue)
  -> Without shell:true, spawnSync throws EINVAL, caught at L249, returns null
  -> queryDistTagsSync always returns null on Windows -> update detection chain broken
Fix: add shell: true to spawnSync options at L239 (queryDistTagsSync) and L259 (queryDistTags)
